From 50fde3e2b2dae7074efc2032b12599fce01f3b9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: packetdeath <packetdeath@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 07:16:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Widen scan offsets to size_t

File positions are size_t; chunk lengths stay 32-bit. CLI_OFF_ANY and
CLI_OFF_NONE become SIZE_MAX and SIZE_MAX - 1 so a real offset below
4 GiB cannot collide with them. Container metadata keeps its 32-bit
"any" value in CLI_CDB_ANY. The bytecode API still receives 32-bit
offsets, narrowed one by one with the "not matched" marker unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
